Z||000041||cadero2dmax||11-09-2001||04:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>sounds like a pretty good plug for the caddy to me.  I dont know what kind of power the 4.9 makes, but Id like to line up next to one some time when my L67 is finished, well mostly because its going to see this....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/fiero10.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Wichita is just a couple hours away from Tulsa, we could meet at Hallett and do a few laps on a COMMA or NASA track day.<P>Both Wichita and Tulsa have very active autocross groups, I would love to take your anchor powered (Ummm. sorry - L67 SBC)Fiero on in that environment.<P>Ohhh, you meant the dragstrip. Just remember one thing, there is more to life than going straight. Even you will have to get that heavy tail end to come around a corner once in a while.<P>Anyway, I honestly have a lot of trouble getting all that lowend 4.9 torque to hook up in a drag environment on my daily driver. That is exactly why, even though I hate automatiecs, the Challenge car will have a low ratio TH125 with 15x10 crag slicks to get it going. But taking that car to the strip against you wouldn't be a fair comparison, though. The Grassroots Motorsports Magazine $2002 Challenge car, while almost street legal, will be built for competition - whereas your car looks like it is built more for street  and showin' off.<BR>So my Mr. Mikes, '88 cradled 4.9 5speed (otherwise looks bone stock) 85 SE would be a more favorable comparison.<P>I'm ready - - when do you want to play in all 3 of the types competition Imentioned above? The forum might be interested in the results.<BR><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>84 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||14
Z||000042||MooCow||11-09-2001||12:12 PM||||Well I just got this information from Rd Parks:<BR>"Ken, we have the parts to install auto versions, except STILL waiting on<BR>the production wiring harnesses. Same for manuals, except we have just<BR>finished the prototype harness and have to install and "proof" it. Then<BR>get it into production.<P>Expected auto kit is $2000 and manual might be $1200 more (depends on<BR>starter used). Install should take 1 week, which equals $2000 in labor.<BR>Lower mileage wrecked Caddy's sell for an average $1600-1800."<P>He also says the reliablility between the two engine are very close and it is a toss up basically.  I am trying to get down there again so that I can actually test drive one.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forum_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000043||cadero2dmax||11-10-2001||10:42 AM||||MooCow<P>Bring that sweet lookin' yellow GT with you to Ed's swap meet in April!! Then you can check out my SE and the Challenge car, both a little different versions of the 4.9 swap.<P><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>86 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||1
Z||000044||jeffndebrus||11-12-2001||01:31 PM||||when will ed parks kits be ready? anyone<BR>also does anyone know what he will charge to do the 4.9 "in house"--total turnkey?||||reg||1
Z||000045||fieroX||11-12-2001||04:28 PM||||cadero2dmax,<BR>sure Ill challenge you, and whats this about L67 sbc?  an L67 is the 3800 series II supercharged v6.  Boat anchor? maybe it is heavy but Ill have no problems taking corners as well as running low 12's no nitrous.  Ill keep everyone updated to my progress, and this summer sometime Id love to meet up and do a race in tulsa.  Should be some good recognition for my website after this goes down.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000046||cadero2dmax||11-12-2001||04:45 PM||||This is just drag racing? The Cadero does a lot more than go straight. I'll challenge your mid 12's (the Cadero has trouble hooking up, low 13's is probably about all it will do) if you will give me equal booking in autocrossing. (See the thread "AUTOCROSS AND SUSPENSIONS" in this forum for my qualifications, and the last autocross car I built).<P>I know exactly what the L67 is, from the Grand Prix, etc. The SBC just "slipped out" in my previous post. That engine weighs a good 80 pounds more than mine. I hope that you know a lot about Fiero suspensions (and how to make one handle in the first place) if you wish to keep it "nimble" with all that weight back there.<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000047||Slammed Fiero||11-12-2001||05:33 PM||||I hope for your sake Fiero X your a good driver and have something more than a stock suspension.<P>you must have a lot of work done to the 3800SC to run low 12's with no NOS. I would hope you would beat a Fiero with a caddy 4.9.<P>As for the autocross portion , I think your in a lot of trouble. The 4.9 may lack some power in respect to the 3800sc , But I'm pretty sure the drivers skill will more than make up for it.<P>You should take a gander at Cadaero2Dmax's old Autocross Fiero. Not exactly a  occasional weekend racer...pretty serious stuff.<P>Just my 2 cents. I think your in for an ass whoopin if it involves corners.<P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000048||Archie||11-12-2001||07:49 PM||||hehe..... I think you need to realize that cadero is "Baiting" you.<P>He has been racing around corners for many years. I would be willing to bet that if he drove a stock 6 cylinder Fiero and YOU drove his cadero, he would STILL beat you.<P>The only way that a race between the 2 cars would be a fair comparison of the abilities of the cars themselves is if both drivers were of the same skill level and both had the same desire to win.<P>IMHO, (if anyone cares) Until that happens a fair comparison between the 2 vehicles cannot be made.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000049||ray b||11-12-2001||08:14 PM||||true that a good driver will win auto-X or drags maybe fairest way would be to let the best driver use each car in turn. <BR>I would love to see a shootout between street tuned[smoged] chevy v-8, caddy 4.9 and N* and a 3800superC on both drag and autoX tracks to see who's got the best allround fiero on pump gas. and whynot a 3.4 turbo and or NOX car tooo.<BR>sure any pure track car on racing fuel/tune willl beat a real street ride, by a bunch too<BR>but got to be real street car for a fair test.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000050||cadero2dmax||11-12-2001||09:00 PM||||Archie, Slammed Fiero, and all - -<P>Yeah, I was just funnin'   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And I should be ashamed of myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>For autocrossing, the 2.8 WOULD still give the 70 or 80 more horsepower in the L67 a run, because it is low end and mid range torque that will win. Power is meaningless in this environment, a 150 horsepower Neon will kill a 300 plus hp Mustang, for example.<P>That is why the lightweight 4.9 is my engine of choice. It pulls like a diesel all the way from idle up to it's limited RPM peak. That is good on an autocross course, bad on a dragstrip. <P>But hey, Archie - - you will still get some of my hard earned cash. If the 4.9 turns out to handle and drive as well as it should, a Finale body is in it's future.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>FieroX, I would love to meet with you. To look both cars over and just compare notes, etc. I owe Paul Herder a visit to pick up some parts (and give him some $ I owe him), so maybe we can get together then. Keep in touch.<P>But I would still like to go racin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>86 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||1
Z||000051||fieroX||11-13-2001||11:01 PM||||It sounds all good to me, Ill autoX race anyone.  I pride myself in being an excellent driver, although I have never raced on a auto X track.  If the weight advantage is only 80 lbs, no big deal, I removed all of my air conditioner equipment and that all added up to about 80 lbs.  Ill keep everyone posted as too my progress, and next summer sometime we will meetup and make an event out of it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000052||Slammed Fiero||11-14-2001||12:30 AM||||HP doesn't mean a thing in an autocross.<P>90% Driver , 10% car. I always giggle when we get guys in Vipers and megabuck sports car come out and make asses of themselves.<P>Stab the gas , kick out the tail , they think their kicking ass. They come in and see a Neon has put them to shame.<P>It won't be a fair competition if you have never autocrossed before. Good driving is a relative term (no offense) George has too many years of experienced driving under his belt.<P>Now.. If you had a third party  Autocross it would be a good comparison. Autocross has too many variables to make it a good measure of car alone. As sad as this sounds a well prepped CRX or civic could come out and kill you both with the right driver.<P><BR>It's all about the driver.<P>JM  ||||reg||1
Z||000053||donalson||11-14-2001||02:30 AM||||what all cars does the 4.9 come in?...anyone got the stats on them?...seems to me now that i live up north near detroit i could prob find a ratty but good running 4.9 car and drive it for a while (daily driver) till i could find a fiero...preferable an 88 5spd  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> mmmm...4.9 fiero daily driver and an mr2 auto-x only car...make a good back up auto-x car for when i'm working on the mr2 hha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>mark<P>------------------<BR>'86 mr2 hardtop<P>mid-engine lover||||reg||1
Z||000054||cadero2dmax||11-14-2001||10:50 AM||||Just for info - - the SCCA is developing a Street Mod 2 class (SM2) that allows 2 seaters. This is where a 4.9 conversion would fit. (and yes, the SBC, 3.8, etc.)<P>The parameters - - the engine must be made by the same manufacturer (GM made the Fiero and all the donors mentioned above, so we are OK). The car must be street legal -doesn't have to be a daily driver, though, just be legal!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> It must have full interior, <P>Lastly the one that kicks my butt. You must have the stock suspension mounting points. In order to locate an '88 cradle in an early chassis, the top of the strut is moved inboard and forward about an inch (each way). So I will probably have to go to E-Mod with the Challenge car, and be uncompetitive again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>But a 4.9 with all that early and mid range grunt - - I may be looking for an '88 coupe chassis soon!!<P>G ||||reg||1
